-- ccc32-nif-c19.l4 -- AMENDMENTS NOT IN FORCE (2026, c. 19 amendments of the Code), from the end of the Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46
-- (lines 19749-19797 of the text: 2026, c. 19, s. 2(2) (adds 3.01(1)(b.1)), s. 4 (replaces 109(1)(b)), s. 24(5) (adds to the definition offence in s 183), s. 28 (adds section 264.01, coercion or control of an intimate partner),
-- s. 42 (adds to the definition secondary designated offence in s 487.04) and s. 45(2) (adds to the definition secondary offence in subsection 490.011(1))).
-- Part ccc32, layer 1. This is a SECOND, FUTURE text of provisions that other parts (ccc4, ccc7, ccc16, ccc17 and the keel's section 3.01) encode in their in-force form: every name here carries `(not in force)`
-- after the section label so that it cannot collide with theirs. NOTHING in this module says the text is law today.
-- WHERE THE TEXT GIVES ONLY THE INSERTED ITEM (ss 2(2), 24(5), 42, 45(2)), the function answers JUST TRUE for section 264.01 and NOTHING for any other offence (points outside the text: the rest of that list is in-force text
-- another part owns, and this part does not reconstruct it). Where it gives the whole replaced paragraph (s 4), it tests membership of the whole paragraph.
-- How a result reads, the naming rule and the rule for days the text leaves open: see the head of ccc32-related-1.l4 and NOTES.md.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30). It is not the official text,
-- and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.

§ `2026, c. 19, s. 2(2) -- paragraph 3.01(1)(b.1) added`

-- 2 (2) Subsection 3.01(1) is amended by adding after paragraph (b): (b.1) an offence under section 264.01 (coercion or control of intimate partner);
-- src:19750 | 2 (2) Subsection 3.01(1) of the Act is amended by adding the following after paragraph (b):
-- src:19751 | (b.1) an offence under section 264.01 (coercion or control of intimate partner);
@ref 2026, c. 19, s. 2(2) (paragraph 3.01(1)(b.1)) (src:19750-19751)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3.01(1)(b.1) (not in force) the offence counts as one in which violence is used, threatened or attempted` MEANS
    IF `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 264.01
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the rest of subsection 3.01(1) is in-force text (the keel's section 3.01), not reconstructed here

§ `2026, c. 19, s. 4 -- paragraph 109(1)(b) replaced`

-- 4 Paragraph 109(1)(b) is replaced by: (b) an offence under subsection 85(1), 85(2), 95(1), 99(1), 100(1), 102(1), 102.1(1), 102.1(2), 103(1) or 104.1(1) or section 264 (criminal harassment) or 264.01 (coercion or control of intimate partner),
-- src:19754 | 4 Paragraph 109(1)(b) of the Act is replaced by the following:
-- src:19755 | (b) an offence under subsection 85(1) (using firearm in commission of offence), 85(2) (using imitation firearm in commission of offence), 95(1) (possession of prohibited or restricted firearm with ammunition), 99(1) (weapons trafficking), 100(1) (possession for purpose of weapons trafficking), 102(1) (making automatic firearm), 102.1(1) (possession of computer data), 102.1(2) (distribution of computer data), 103(1) (importing or exporting knowing it is unauthorized) or 104.1(1) (altering cartridge magazine) or section 264 (criminal harassment) or 264.01 (coercion or control of intimate partner),
@ref 2026, c. 19, s. 4 (paragraph 109(1)(b)) (src:19754-19755)
GIVEN `the offence charged` IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 109(1)(b) (not in force) the offence is one listed in paragraph (b)` MEANS
    IF `the offence is one of the subsections, or one of the sections, that paragraph (b) names`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (b) names the offences it lists and does not say it lists nothing else
    WHERE
        `the offence is one of the subsections, or one of the sections, that paragraph (b) names` MEANS
                (`the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 85 AND (`the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR `the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            OR  (`the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 95 AND `the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
            OR  (`the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 99 AND `the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
            OR  (`the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 100 AND `the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
            OR  (`the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 102 AND `the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
            OR  (`the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 102.1 AND (`the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)" OR `the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(2)"))
            OR  (`the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 103 AND `the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
            OR  (`the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 104.1 AND `the offence charged`'s `subsection` EQUALS "(1)")
            OR  `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 264
            OR  `the offence charged`'s `section` EQUALS 264.01

