§ `2026, c. 19, s. 28 -- section 264.01 added: coercion or control of intimate partner`

-- 28 The Act is amended by adding the following after section 264: 264.01 (1) Everyone commits an offence who engages in a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct referred to in subsection (2),
-- with intent to cause their intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner's safety is threatened or knowing that, or being reckless as to whether, the pattern ... would cause their intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner's safety is threatened.
-- "intimate partner" is the section 2 term: its answer is an input carried through as a MAYBE BOOLEAN. "Everyone commits an offence who ..." is neither "if" nor "only if" nor a flat negative: where an element is not met the answer is NOTHING
-- (limited by its own wording), a marginal reading for a lawyer (the other reading: the elements are necessary and sufficient, so JUST FALSE).
-- src:19762 | 28 The Act is amended by adding the following after section 264:
-- src:19763 | Coercion or control of intimate partner
-- src:19764 | 264.01 (1) Everyone commits an offence who engages in a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct referred to in subsection (2), with intent to cause their intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety is threatened or knowing that, or being reckless as to whether, the pattern of coercive or controlling conduct would cause their intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety is threatened.
-- src:19765 | Pattern of coercive or controlling conduct
-- src:19766 | (2) A pattern of coercive or controlling conduct consists of any combination, or repeated instances, of any of the following acts:
-- src:19767 | (a) using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence against
-- src:19768 | (i) the intimate partner,
-- src:19769 | (ii) any person under the age of 18 who is the intimate partner’s child or who is in the intimate partner’s lawful care or charge,
-- src:19770 | (iii) any other person known to the intimate partner, or
-- src:19771 | (iv) any animal that is known to the intimate partner;
-- src:19772 | (b) coercing or attempting to coerce the intimate partner to engage in sexual activity;
-- src:19773 | (c) engaging in any other conduct — including conduct listed in any of the following subparagraphs — if, in all the circumstances, the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause the intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, is threatened:
-- src:19774 | (i) controlling, attempting to control or monitoring the intimate partner’s location, movements, actions or social interactions, including by a means of telecommunication,
-- src:19775 | (ii) controlling or attempting to control the manner in which the intimate partner cares for any person under the age of 18 referred to in subparagraph (a)(ii) or any animal referred to in subparagraph (a)(iv),
-- src:19776 | (iii) controlling or attempting to control any matter related to the intimate partner’s employment or education,
-- src:19777 | (iv) controlling or attempting to control the intimate partner’s finances or other property or monitoring their finances,
-- src:19778 | (v) controlling or attempting to control the intimate partner’s expression of gender, physical appearance, manner of dress, diet, taking of medication or access to health services or to medication,
-- src:19779 | (vi) controlling or attempting to control the intimate partner’s expression of their thoughts, their opinions, their religious, spiritual or other beliefs, or their culture, including the intimate partner’s use of their language or their access to their linguistic, religious, spiritual or cultural community,
-- src:19780 | (vii) threatening to die by suicide or to self-harm, or
-- src:19781 | (viii) damaging, or threatening or attempting to damage, the intimate partner’s property or the property of anyone known to them.
-- src:19782 | Circumstances
-- src:19783 | (3) The circumstances referred to in paragraph (2)(c) include the nature of the relationship between the accused and the intimate partner, in particular whether the intimate partner is in a position of vulnerability in relation to the accused and whether the accused manipulated the intimate partner by targeting their vulnerabilities.
-- src:19784 | Punishment
-- src:19785 | (4) Everyone who commits an offence under this section is
-- src:19786 | (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or
-- src:19787 | (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- src:19788 | For greater certainty
-- src:19789 | (5) For the purposes of this section, and for greater certainty, a person’s safety includes their psychological safety.
@ref 2026, c. 19, s. 28 (adding section 264.01) (src:19762-19789)
GIVEN `the accused engaged in a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct referred to in subsection (2), as that subsection answers` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused acted with intent to cause their intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused acted knowing that the pattern would cause their intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused acted being reckless as to whether the pattern would cause their intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2 intimate partner: the person subjected to the pattern is the accused’s intimate partner` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264.01(1) (not in force) the accused commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the accused acted with intent to cause their intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety is threatened`
                OR `the accused acted knowing that the pattern would cause their intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety is threatened`
                OR `the accused acted being reckless as to whether the pattern would cause their intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety is threatened`)
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "with intent to cause their intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety is threatened or knowing that, or being reckless as to whether"
        IF `the accused engaged in a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct referred to in subsection (2), as that subsection answers` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Everyone commits an offence who engages in a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct referred to in subsection (2)"
        IF `the accused engaged in a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct referred to in subsection (2), as that subsection answers` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether subsection (2) is met is not covered
        IF `s 2 intimate partner: the person subjected to the pattern is the accused’s intimate partner` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an intimate partner is for section 2 "intimate partner", whose answer is not JUST TRUE

-- (2) A pattern of coercive or controlling conduct consists of any combination, or repeated instances, of any of the following acts: (a) violence; (b) coercing sexual activity; (c) any other conduct, if it could reasonably be expected to cause the intimate partner to believe their safety is threatened.
-- The facts are a count of acts under each paragraph. A pattern needs "any combination, or repeated instances": at least two acts in all (fork F6 in NOTES.md); "consists of" is read as a definition, so fewer than two is the text's no (marginal reading).
@ref s 264.01(2) (not in force) (src:19765-19766)
DECLARE `s 264.01(2) (not in force) acts` HAS
    `the number of acts within paragraph (a): using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence against a person or animal named in it` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of acts within paragraph (b): coercing or attempting to coerce the intimate partner to engage in sexual activity` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of acts within paragraph (c): any other conduct that could reasonably be expected to cause the intimate partner to believe their safety is threatened` IS A NUMBER

@ref s 264.01(2) (not in force) (src:19765-19766)
GIVEN acts IS A `s 264.01(2) (not in force) acts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264.01(2) (not in force) the acts make up a pattern of coercive or controlling conduct` MEANS
    IF acts's `the number of acts within paragraph (a): using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence against a person or animal named in it`
       PLUS acts's `the number of acts within paragraph (b): coercing or attempting to coerce the intimate partner to engage in sexual activity`
       PLUS acts's `the number of acts within paragraph (c): any other conduct that could reasonably be expected to cause the intimate partner to believe their safety is threatened`
       AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A pattern of coercive or controlling conduct consists of any combination, or repeated instances, of any of the following acts"

-- (2)(a) using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence against (i) the intimate partner, (ii) any person under 18 who is the intimate partner's child or in their lawful care or charge, (iii) any other person known to the intimate partner, or (iv) any animal known to the intimate partner.
@ref s 264.01(2)(a) (not in force) (src:19767-19771)
DECLARE `s 264.01(2)(a) (not in force) the target of the act` IS ONE OF
    `s 264.01(2)(a)(i) (not in force) the intimate partner`
    `s 264.01(2)(a)(ii) (not in force) any person under the age of 18 who is the intimate partner’s child or who is in the intimate partner’s lawful care or charge`
    `s 264.01(2)(a)(iii) (not in force) any other person known to the intimate partner`
    `s 264.01(2)(a)(iv) (not in force) any animal that is known to the intimate partner`
    `s 264.01(2)(a) (not in force) another target`

@ref s 264.01(2)(a) (not in force) (src:19767-19771)
GIVEN `the act is using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence` IS A BOOLEAN
      target IS A `s 264.01(2)(a) (not in force) the target of the act`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264.01(2)(a) (not in force) the act is within paragraph (a)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act is using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence against"
        IF target EQUALS `s 264.01(2)(a) (not in force) another target` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "using, attempting to use or threatening to use violence against"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (2)(b) coercing or attempting to coerce the intimate partner to engage in sexual activity.
@ref s 264.01(2)(b) (not in force) (src:19772)
GIVEN `the accused coerced or attempted to coerce the intimate partner to engage in sexual activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264.01(2)(b) (not in force) the act is within paragraph (b)` MEANS
    IF `the accused coerced or attempted to coerce the intimate partner to engage in sexual activity`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "coercing or attempting to coerce the intimate partner to engage in sexual activity"

-- (2)(c) engaging in any other conduct -- including conduct listed in any of the following subparagraphs -- if, in all the circumstances, the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause the intimate partner to believe that
-- the intimate partner's safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, is threatened: (i) to (viii). The "if" is the text's condition: where it fails the text says no. The subparagraphs are examples ("including"): conduct not named in them is still within (c).
@ref s 264.01(2)(c) (not in force) (src:19773-19781)
GIVEN `in all the circumstances, the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause the intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, is threatened` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264.01(2)(c) (not in force) the conduct is within paragraph (c)` MEANS
    IF `in all the circumstances, the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause the intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, is threatened`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if, in all the circumstances, the conduct could reasonably be expected to cause the intimate partner to believe that the intimate partner’s safety, or the safety of anyone known to them, is threatened"

@ref s 264.01(2)(c)(i) to (viii) (not in force) (src:19774-19781)
DECLARE `s 264.01(2)(c) (not in force) the conduct` IS ONE OF
    `s 264.01(2)(c)(i) (not in force) controlling, attempting to control or monitoring the intimate partner’s location, movements, actions or social interactions, including by a means of telecommunication`
    `s 264.01(2)(c)(ii) (not in force) controlling or attempting to control the manner in which the intimate partner cares for any person under the age of 18 referred to in subparagraph (a)(ii) or any animal referred to in subparagraph (a)(iv)`
    `s 264.01(2)(c)(iii) (not in force) controlling or attempting to control any matter related to the intimate partner’s employment or education`
    `s 264.01(2)(c)(iv) (not in force) controlling or attempting to control the intimate partner’s finances or other property or monitoring their finances`
    `s 264.01(2)(c)(v) (not in force) controlling or attempting to control the intimate partner’s expression of gender, physical appearance, manner of dress, diet, taking of medication or access to health services or to medication`
    `s 264.01(2)(c)(vi) (not in force) controlling or attempting to control the intimate partner’s expression of their thoughts, their opinions, their religious, spiritual or other beliefs, or their culture, including the intimate partner’s use of their language or their access to their linguistic, religious, spiritual or cultural community`
    `s 264.01(2)(c)(vii) (not in force) threatening to die by suicide or to self-harm`
    `s 264.01(2)(c)(viii) (not in force) damaging, or threatening or attempting to damage, the intimate partner’s property or the property of anyone known to them`
    `s 264.01(2)(c) (not in force) other conduct not listed in subparagraphs (i) to (viii)`

@ref s 264.01(2)(c)(i) to (viii) (not in force) (src:19774-19781)
GIVEN conduct IS A `s 264.01(2)(c) (not in force) the conduct`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264.01(2)(c) (not in force) the conduct is listed in one of the subparagraphs` MEANS
    CONSIDER conduct
    WHEN `s 264.01(2)(c)(i) (not in force) controlling, attempting to control or monitoring the intimate partner’s location, movements, actions or social interactions, including by a means of telecommunication` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 264.01(2)(c)(ii) (not in force) controlling or attempting to control the manner in which the intimate partner cares for any person under the age of 18 referred to in subparagraph (a)(ii) or any animal referred to in subparagraph (a)(iv)` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 264.01(2)(c)(iii) (not in force) controlling or attempting to control any matter related to the intimate partner’s employment or education` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 264.01(2)(c)(iv) (not in force) controlling or attempting to control the intimate partner’s finances or other property or monitoring their finances` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 264.01(2)(c)(v) (not in force) controlling or attempting to control the intimate partner’s expression of gender, physical appearance, manner of dress, diet, taking of medication or access to health services or to medication` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 264.01(2)(c)(vi) (not in force) controlling or attempting to control the intimate partner’s expression of their thoughts, their opinions, their religious, spiritual or other beliefs, or their culture, including the intimate partner’s use of their language or their access to their linguistic, religious, spiritual or cultural community` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 264.01(2)(c)(vii) (not in force) threatening to die by suicide or to self-harm` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 264.01(2)(c)(viii) (not in force) damaging, or threatening or attempting to damage, the intimate partner’s property or the property of anyone known to them` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 264.01(2)(c) (not in force) other conduct not listed in subparagraphs (i) to (viii)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including conduct listed in any of the following subparagraphs"

-- (3) The circumstances referred to in paragraph (2)(c) include the nature of the relationship between the accused and the intimate partner, in particular whether the intimate partner is in a position of vulnerability in relation to the accused
-- and whether the accused manipulated the intimate partner by targeting their vulnerabilities.
@ref s 264.01(3) (not in force) (src:19782-19783)
DECLARE `s 264.01(3) (not in force) the circumstance` IS ONE OF
    `s 264.01(3) (not in force) the nature of the relationship between the accused and the intimate partner`
    `s 264.01(3) (not in force) whether the intimate partner is in a position of vulnerability in relation to the accused`
    `s 264.01(3) (not in force) whether the accused manipulated the intimate partner by targeting their vulnerabilities`
    `s 264.01(3) (not in force) another circumstance`

@ref s 264.01(3) (not in force) (src:19782-19783)
GIVEN circumstance IS A `s 264.01(3) (not in force) the circumstance`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264.01(3) (not in force) the circumstances referred to in paragraph (2)(c) include the circumstance` MEANS
    CONSIDER circumstance
    WHEN `s 264.01(3) (not in force) the nature of the relationship between the accused and the intimate partner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 264.01(3) (not in force) whether the intimate partner is in a position of vulnerability in relation to the accused` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 264.01(3) (not in force) whether the accused manipulated the intimate partner by targeting their vulnerabilities` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 264.01(3) (not in force) another circumstance` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The circumstances referred to in paragraph (2)(c) include"

-- (4) Everyone who commits an offence under this section is (a) guilty of an indictable offence and liable to imprisonment for a term of not more than 10 years; or (b) guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
-- The summary limb states no penalty: the general penalty of section 787(1) is taken as an INPUT (a Punishment, part ccc29).
@ref s 264.01(4) (not in force) (src:19784-19787)
GIVETH A `Class of offence`
`s 264.01(4) (not in force) the class of the offence` MEANS `an offence that the section makes both indictable and punishable on summary conviction`

@ref s 264.01(4) (not in force) (src:19784-19787)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of proceeding`
      `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction` IS A Punishment
GIVETH A Punishment
`s 264.01(4) (not in force) the punishment for the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `by indictment` THEN
        Punishment WITH
            `mode` IS `by indictment`
            `maximum imprisonment` IS `imprisonment for a term of` `ten years`
            `minimum imprisonment` IS `no imprisonment is stated`
            `maximum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
            `minimum fine` IS `no fine is stated`
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `s 787(1) the general penalty for an offence punishable on summary conviction`

-- (5) For the purposes of this section, and for greater certainty, a person's safety includes their psychological safety.
@ref s 264.01(5) (not in force) (src:19788-19789)
DECLARE `s 264.01(5) (not in force) the kind of safety` IS ONE OF
    `s 264.01(5) (not in force) psychological safety`
    `s 264.01(5) (not in force) another kind of safety`

@ref s 264.01(5) (not in force) (src:19788-19789)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 264.01(5) (not in force) the kind of safety`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 264.01(5) (not in force) a person’s safety includes the kind of safety` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 264.01(5) (not in force) psychological safety` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 264.01(5) (not in force) another kind of safety` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a person’s safety includes their psychological safety"

